{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"call_696020c1ba034350a24445dd","toolName":"bash","args":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788550545620164410-fixer && powder take if-critic-silent-canopy-config --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\" 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\""},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\",\"title\":\"Malformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\",\"repo\":\"misty-step/canopy\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"lease\":{\"agent\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"principal\":\"none\",\"until\":\"2026-09-04T23:08:57.104Z\"},\"ask\":null,\"proof\":null,\"abandoned\":false,\"notes\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T18:54:31.392Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: main.go:37-41 — when -config is absent, a malformed canopy.json (decode or validation error from LoadInventory) is silently discarded and Canopy starts with zero instances and defaults; no error is logged or surfaced. This contradicts the stated rejection policy at inventory.go:16-17 (\\\"Unknown fields are rejected so a misspelled operational setting cannot silently select a default\\\") and the loud log.Fatalf behavior of the -config path at main.go:31-33.\\nRequired: a default canopy.json that fails to load must fail loudly (or be surfaced to the operator), matching the -config path behavior.\\nProposed spec direction: treat an existing but unparseable default canopy.json as a fatal startup error, identical to -config; keep the true zero-config (no file) path unchanged.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:54:31.226Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\n"}],"details":{}}}
