 inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:54:31.226Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nexit=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550587909}]}
