 [--agent AGENT]\n  powder set-repo ID [--repo REPO|--clear] [--agent AGENT]\n  powder set-blockers ID [--blocked-by a,b|--clear] [--agent AGENT]\n  powder use URL [--agent AGENT]\n  powder doctor [--agent AGENT]\n  powder version\n  powder skill\n\nEnvironment: POWDER_URL; POWDER_API_KEY\nClient config: ~/.config/powder/config. JSON on stdout. list/show --plain for text. Errors are JSON on stderr with a code.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550576772},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_056f0154a68e4a12912aaf3a","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"repo: misty-step/canopy\nagents:\n  builder:  { poll: \"./forest poll builder\",  interval: 300 }\n  verifier: { poll: \"./forest poll verifier\", interval: 120 }\n  fixer:    { poll: \"./forest poll fixer\",    interval: 300 }\n  critic:   { poll: \"./agents/critic/poll.sh\", interval: 86400 }\n  tester:   { poll: \"./agents/tester/poll.sh\", interval: 86400 }\nchecks:\n  - name: test\n    run: go test ./...\n  - name: vet\n    run: go vet ./...\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550576772},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The repo is `misty-step/canopy`. POWDER_AGENT is `forest-misty-step/canopy`. Let me run powder doctor, then list --mine, then show the job, then take it.\n\nThe subject id is `if-critic-silent-canopy-config` (from the request payload \"subject\":\"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\"). Wait — the payload subject is \"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\". Hmm, but typically subject is an ID like a number for github. For powder, the job id probably is `if-critic-silent-canopy-config` or something else.\n\nActually wait, let me re-read the request payload:\n```json\n{\"schema\":\"forest.review-request.v2\",\"subject\":\"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\",\"branch\":\"forest/if-critic-silent-canopy-config/fail-loud-default-config\",\"revision\":\"0b6189b97ab043ea94fd5ff301cd2f0903990fb4\",\"time\":\"2026-09-04T19:09:32Z\",\"tracker\":\"powder\"}\n```\n\nSo subj