ject from the request. The subject is `if-critic-silent-canopy-config`. Maybe the job id is different. Let me try `powder show if-critic-silent-canopy-config` or list all jobs.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"No jobs in powder list under my agent or takeable. Since the request has `tracker: powder`, and there's no Powder job... Hmm. Let me check `powder show` with the subject from the request. The subject is `if-critic-silent-canopy-config`. Maybe the job id is different. Let me try `powder show if-critic-silent-canopy-config` or list all jobs.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_c3bd7b7d19ac4b76aa0dc043","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788550545620164410-fixer && powder list --repo misty-step/canopy --limit 100 2>&1 | head -80"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cd357904ab6849eea45e0a6b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788550545620164410-fixer && powder show if-critic-silent-canopy-config --plain 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":54,"output":268,"cacheRead":16128,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":86,"totalTokens":16450,"cost":{"input":0.0000027000000000000004,"output":0.0000268,"cacheRead":0.00016128,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00019078}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788550582605,"responseId":"gen-1788550582-F3UkCkkhek2T1UGlhZZJ","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c3bd7b7d19ac4b76aa0dc043","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"jobs\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"if-fleet-observability-projection\",\n      \"title\": \"External single-pane visibility across repository Forests\",\n      \"spec\": \"Purpose: give human operators one simple, beautiful, near-real-time pane for configuration and current operations across one or more independent Iron Forest instances. The pane is an operator-owned external projection. Iron Forest remains headless and the Kernel does not serve UI.\\n\\nBoundary:\\n- Collect only supported forest.cli.v2 read surfaces through explicit local or SSH routes. Never read .forest files directly.\\n- Keep independent Kernels independent. Add no coordination authority, mutation endpoint, durable event store, implicit discovery, or shared credentials.\\n- Keep the first implementation read-only. Publication beyond the operator machine requires explicit authority.\\n- An unreachable source is UNKNOWN, never healthy or empty. Show collection time, source identity, and freshness for every instance.\\n\\nSingle-pane contract:\\n- Fleet strip: repository, host/profile identity, forest version, reachability, Kernel state, active Run count, audit result, recent failure signal, last observed time, and staleness.\\n- Selected instance: resolved primary and checks; declaration roster and relevant resolved configuration; Kernel running/running-known state; live Runs with elapsed time; each trigger's state-known, running-known, Poll result, Run error, Poll error, audit error, last Run, and interval; audit baseline/audited revision/result/violations; whole-Ledger aggregates; recent Runs and failure reasons.\\n- Keep Poll result and dispatched Run outcome as separate dimensions. Read intervals from config show and aggregates from status.ledger.\\n- Fetch Run logs on demand through forest run logs --json. A completed Ledger row whose log was evicted returns CLI exit 0 with data.complete=true and data.retained=false; render that as the expected no-retained-log state. Reserve CLI exit 4 for an unknown Run identity with neither a Ledger row nor log. Never infer log presence from Ledger row age or position.\\n- Preserve every forest.cli.v2 envelope exit/error. A failed command must produce an explicit source error, not a partial healthy view.\\n\\nSelected architecture:\\n- Build one external Go process. Use the standard library for process execution, SSH invocation, HTTP, and html/template. Vendor the HTMX browser asset; use no npm toolchain.\\n- Render server-owned HTML fragments enhanced with HTMX. Keep only ephemeral snapshots in memory.\\n- Poll selected-instance read surfaces on a bounded two-second cadence and fleet summaries less often. Use server-sent events only while a live log drawer is open; do not invent a Kernel event API.\\n- Keep all routes read-only. The pane may select instances, filter Runs, refresh, and open logs; it does not cancel Runs, reset triggers, mutate trackers, or change configuration.\\n\\nFirst proof:\\n- Run outside Kernel modules against one real local instance and one deliberately unreachable inventory entry.\\n- Render current forest.cli.v2 data without fabricated values, including unknown/error states and the observed distinction between a successful Builder Poll and a failed Builder Run.\\n- Update visible instance state within two seconds of collection; show disconnected and stale states when collection stops.\\n- Open one retained Run log, show one completed Run with data.retained=false, and show one unknown Run identity returning CLI exit 4.\\n- Exercise keyboard and pointer navigation at desktop width; prevent horizontal clipping at narrow width.\\n- Measure collector command frequency and page update behavior. Do not add durable ingestion or fleet control unless this proof names an operator question snapshots cannot answer.\\n\\nAcceptance:\\n- One external pane answers: Which instances are reachable? What is running now? What failed? Is the audited primary trustworthy? What configuration and declarations are active? How fresh is each answer?\\n- The proof has no Kernel changes beyond supported read-surface corrections, no mutation routes, no second store, no npm build, and no hidden direct-file integration.\\n- Live-scenario evidence records exact commands, timestamps, source revisions, UI results, and failure handling.\",\n      \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"blocked_by\": [\n        \"if-293\"\n      ],\n      \"lease\": null,\n      \"ask\": null,\n      \"proof\": \"Published https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/commit/ae3d2b7. go test -race ./..., go vet ./..., go build, and node --check static/htmx.min.js passed. Live browser at 127.0.0.1:8080 read 1,196 Ledger Runs from current forest.cli.v2, preserved builder poll OK versus Run ERROR, rendered local fresh plus unreachable unknown, and showed retained, known-evicted, and unknown log states. HTMX 2.0.9 selection/poll swaps, keyboard focus order, 1440px desktop, and 390px mobile with no document overflow were exercised.\",\n      \"abandoned\": false,\n      \"notes\": [\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-01T23:13:55.673Z\",\n          \"by\": \"Main\",\n          \"text\": \"Operator direction 2026-09-01: many repository Forests and high agent throughput need a human-scale account of what is happening—within one project, across projects, and across agents. This is an observability projection over independent Kernels, not a dashboard, coordinator, or second authority inside Iron Forest.\\n\\nAfter `if-293` stabilizes one instance's JSON health/read surfaces, design an external Field Station-style projection. Start with an explicit inventory plus read-only SSH/local calls to `forest version/config/declaration/status/audit/run` JSON, exact Git revisions/evidence, and tracker summaries through each repository profile's CLI. Render source identity, roster/config drift, active and failed Runs, throughput/trends, accepted/rejected work, changed product/system narrative, unresolved decisions, costs when attributable, deployment state when supplied, and UNKNOWN for unreachable sources. Separate observed/evidenced/inferred/unknown claims. Preserve Misty Step and R90 access boundaries and publish nothing without operator authority.\\n\\nFirst proof: static report, no service or new database. Measure whether snapshot collection can answer operator questions and stay current. Introduce durable event ingestion only after the report names a question snapshots cannot answer. Keep this spec-less until the target repositories, projection owner/repository, retention, and publication boundary are chosen.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:00:06.664Z\",\n          \"by\": \"none\",\n          \"text\": \"Operator clarification 2026-09-02: Iron Forest remains primarily headless, but human operators require one simple, beautiful, near-real-time pane for configuration and current operations across one or more instances. The projection may be HTML or HTMX and may live outside Iron Forest. Preserve independent Kernels and forest.cli.v2 JSON over local/SSH collection as source truth; do not add coordination authority or a second store. Replace the blanket no-dashboard framing with a boundary: no UI server in the Kernel. First design decision is raw-HTML client rendering versus an external HTMX fragment server; prove one-instance accuracy, unknown/error states, live Runs, trigger Poll-vs-Run status, audit state, configuration, and best-effort retained logs before fleet expansion.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:10:05.765Z\",\n          \"by\": \"none\",\n          \"text\": \"Operator selected external Go + HTMX for the first live proof on 2026-09-02. Raw HTML remains the rejected comparison direction. Keep the collector/read-surface contract identical; server-render fragments, vendor HTMX, use no npm, retain no durable projection state, and expose no mutation routes.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:14:22.741Z\",\n          \"by\": \"none\",\n          \"text\": \"Accuracy correction from the current 1,168-row Ledger: historical aggregate agents are not limited to the configured roster and include blank and legacy/composite identities such as beaver,owl. The pane must derive Run filters and aggregate rows from returned data, not hardcode declaration names. Render blank identities as Unknown/legacy and non-roster identities as Historical/legacy while keeping the current declaration roster separate. Current observed whole-Ledger pass_rate is 0.6712328767123288; never substitute prototype metrics.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:41:34.699Z\",\n          \"by\": \"none\",\n          \"text\": \"Repository boundary selected by the operator: Canopy is a separate misty-step/canopy codebase. Iron Forest owns forest.cli.v2; Canopy owns explicit inventory, local/SSH collection, in-memory freshness state, Go HTTP/templates, vendored HTMX, and the read-only single pane. Integration is command/schema based, never Go imports or direct .forest reads.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:58:21.028Z\",\n          \"by\": \"canopy-prototype\",\n          \"text\": \"took\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T18:28:34.352Z\",\n          \"by\": \"canopy-prototype\",\n          \"text\": \"done: Published https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/commit/ae3d2b7. go test -race ./..., go vet ./..., go build, and node --check static/htmx.min.js passed. Live browser at 127.0.0.1:8080 read 1,196 Ledger Runs from current forest.cli.v2, preserved builder poll OK versus Run ERROR, rendered local fresh plus unreachable unknown, and showed retained, known-evicted, and unknown log states. HTMX 2.0.9 selection/poll swaps, keyboard focus order, 1440px desktop, and 390px mobile with no document overflow were exercised.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"at\": \"2026-09-02T18:39:32.49Z\",\n          \"by\": \"canopy-prototype\",\n          \"text\": \"Post-proof correction published at https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/commit/feadbcf: log placeholders now use stable hx-preserve identities. Browser proof opened retained Run 1788371452917134761-builder, waited 5.2 seconds across multiple 2-second instance swaps, and observed the same drawer node and retained state.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"created_by\": null,\n      \"promoted_by\": null,\n      \"promoted_at\": null,\n      \"promotions\": [],\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-09-01T23:13:55.257Z\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-02T18:39:32.49Z\",\n      \"derived\": {\n        \"terminal\": true,\n        \"waiting\": false,\n        \"open\": false,\n        \"live\": false,\n        \"takeable\": false\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"canopy-operational-multi-repo\",\n      \"title\": \"Operate Canopy across real repository Forests\",\n      \"spec\": \"Purpose: turn the completed Canopy prototype into an operator-used pane over multiple real repository Forests.\\n\\nScope:\\n- Configure an explicit inventory with at least two reachable Forest instances from different repositories through supported local or SSH forest.cli.v2 routes.\\n- Keep Canopy read-only, ephemeral, and independent of every Kernel. Add no mutation route, direct .forest read, shared credential, implicit discovery, coordination authority, or durable projection store.\\n- Record the operator-selected access and publication boundary before binding beyond loopback. Protect any non-loopback listener because Run logs can contain sensitive repository output.\\n- Exercise the existing fleet, selected-instance, trigger Poll-versus-Run, audit, configuration, declaration, Ledger, freshness, and log views against the real inventory. Preserve explicit UNKNOWN and stale states for unavailable sources.\\n\\nAcceptance:\\n- One operator-used Canopy process shows at least two reachable repository Forests and answers which instances are reachable, what is running, what failed, whether each audited primary is trustworthy, which configuration and declarations are active, and how fresh each answer is.\\n- No Kernel code, projection mutation path, second store, direct file integration, or npm toolchain is introduced.\\n- Proof records the exact Canopy revision, inventory identities with secrets removed, listener/access boundary, commands and timestamps, and browser results for desktop and narrow widths. Publication beyond the operator machine occurs only with explicit operator authority.\",\n      \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"blocked_by\": [\n        \"if-fleet-observability-projection\"\n      ],\n      \"lease\": null,\n      \"ask\": null,\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550585417},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_cd357904ab6849eea45e0a6b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"id\tif-critic-silent-canopy-config\nstate\tlive\ntitle\tMalformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\nrepo\tmisty-step/canopy\ncreated_by\tnone\npromoted_by\tnone\npromoted_at\t2026-09-04T19:04:07Z\nspec\n## Problem\n\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\n\n## Required behavior\n\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\n\n## Proof\n\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\nnote\t2026-09-04T18:54:31Z\tforest-misty-step/iron-forest\tfiled-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\nObserved: main.go:37-41 — when -config is absent, a malformed canopy.json (decode or validation error from LoadInventory) is silently discarded and Canopy starts with zero instances and defaults; no error is logged or surfaced. This contradicts the stated rejection policy at inventory.go:16-17 (\"Unknown fields are rejected so a misspelled operational setting cannot silently select a default\") and the loud log.Fatalf behavior of the -config path at main.go:31-33.\nRequired: a default canopy.json that fails to load must fail loudly (or be surfaced to the operator), matching the -config path behavior.\nProposed spec direction: treat an existing but unparseable default canopy.json as a fatal startup error, identical to -config; keep the true zero-config (no file) path unchanged.\nnote\t2026-09-04T19:08:57Z\tforest-misty-step/iron-forest\ttook\nexit=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550585417},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Powder job `if-critic-silent-canopy-config` exists, is live (taken with a note \"took\" at 2026-09-04T19:08:57Z). But the task says \"take\" the job with the private claim. I'm a Fixer, so I need to take/resume the job by job id. Since the job is live (held), the CLI would return `held` unless the CLI presents that job's matching stored claim, which resumes it.\n\nLet me try `powder take if-critic-silent-canopy-config --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\"` — per skill: \"A Fixer uses the same Subject's private claim by job id before branch mutation\". The CLI resumes by job id using the stored private claim. Let me run it.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The Powder job `if-critic-silent-canopy-config` exists, is live (taken with a note \\\"took\\\" at 2026-09-04T19:08:57Z). But the task says \\\"take\\\" the job with the private claim. I'm a Fixer, so I need to take/resume the job by job id. Since the job is live (held), the CLI would return `held` unless the CLI presents that job's matching stored claim, which resumes it.\\n\\nLet me try `powder take if-critic-silent-canopy-config --agent \\\"$POWDER_AGENT\\\"` — per skill: \\\"A Fixer uses the same Subject's private claim by job id before branch mutation\\\". The CLI resumes by job id using the stored private claim. Let me run it.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"text","text":"The Powder job `if-critic-silent-canopy-config` exists and is live. As the Fixer, I must take/resume it with the private claim before mutating the branch."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_696020c1ba034350a24445dd","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/phaedrus/development/misty-step/canopy/.forest/worktrees/1788550545620164410-fixer && powder take if-critic-silent-canopy-config --agent \"$POWDER_AGENT\" 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731","usage":{"input":3447,"output":317,"cacheRead":16384,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":155,"totalTokens":20148,"cost":{"input":0.00017235000000000002,"output":0.000031700000000000005,"cacheRead":0.00016384,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00036789000000000006}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788550585418,"responseId":"gen-1788550585-bAOMA5vezMdwgC4zXPCF","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_696020c1ba034350a24445dd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"id\":\"if-critic-silent-canopy-config\",\"title\":\"Malformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\",\"repo\":\"misty-step/canopy\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"lease\":{\"agent\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"principal\":\"none\",\"until\":\"2026-09-04T23:08:57.104Z\"},\"ask\":null,\"proof\":null,\"abandoned\":false,\"notes\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T18:54:31.392Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"filed-by: forest-misty-step/iron-forest @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: worktree 1788548005453810023-critic, unknown (no forest binary in worktree; forest version unavailable)\\nObserved: main.go:37-41 — when -config is absent, a malformed canopy.json (decode or validation error from LoadInventory) is silently discarded and Canopy starts with zero instances and defaults; no error is logged or surfaced. This contradicts the stated rejection policy at inventory.go:16-17 (\\\"Unknown fields are rejected so a misspelled operational setting cannot silently select a default\\\") and the loud log.Fatalf behavior of the -config path at main.go:31-33.\\nRequired: a default canopy.json that fails to load must fail loudly (or be surfaced to the operator), matching the -config path behavior.\\nProposed spec direction: treat an existing but unparseable default canopy.json as a fatal startup error, identical to -config; keep the true zero-config (no file) path unchanged.\"},{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\"by\":\"forest-misty-step/iron-forest\",\"text\":\"took\"}],\"created_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_by\":\"none\",\"promoted_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\"promotions\":[{\"at\":\"2026-09-04T19:04:07.457Z\",\"by\":\"none\",\"spec\":\"## Problem\\n\\nWhen `-config` is absent and a regular `canopy.json` exists, `main` discards every `LoadInventory` error and continues with an empty inventory. Explicit operator configuration can therefore silently become zero-config discovery. The explicit `-config` path already fails loudly.\\n\\n## Required behavior\\n\\n- If default `canopy.json` is absent, preserve zero-config discovery.\\n- If default `canopy.json` exists as a regular file, load it through `LoadInventory`; any read, decode, trailing JSON, unknown-field, or validation error must terminate startup through the same `load inventory:` boundary as explicit `-config`.\\n- Keep explicit `-config` behavior unchanged.\\n- Align the README precedence statement in `canopy-docs-discovery-alignment` with the corrected behavior before that documentation is completed.\\n\\n## Proof\\n\\nRun the actual Canopy process from a temporary directory with malformed `canopy.json`, no `-config`, and a safe ephemeral listen address. It exits nonzero, stderr contains `load inventory:`, and no server starts. A companion run with no file starts zero-config and returns 200 from `/healthz`. Existing inventory tests pass.\"}],\"created_at\":\"2026-09-04T18:54:31.226Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-04T19:08:57.104Z\",\"derived\":{\"terminal\":false,\"waiting\":false,\"open\":true,\"live\":true,\"takeable\":false}}\nexit=0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550587909},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `powder take` succeeded (exit 0) and retur